# Line-ending policy: store AND check out text files as LF on every platform.
#
# FlyingSquirrel runs on Linux — the companion computer (Pi/Jetson), the CI
# runners, and the Docker images. A Windows checkout's CRLF would otherwise
# break shell-script shebangs ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M"),
# Dockerfile RUN steps, and the systemd unit on the target. `eol=lf` pins LF
# in the working tree too, so the committed bytes are identical everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders for the files that MUST be LF to execute on Linux.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# PowerShell tolerates LF, so the .ps1 stays LF too (covered by the rule above).
